    "body": "## Summary\n\nReferences #820. This documentation-only principal investigation responds to the owner request for a whole-project geometric-attention programme rather than another isolated test-repair gate.\n\n- Reconstruct current and historical model paths, including dormant geometry, memory, runtime, imported research and product surfaces.\n- Include independent mathematics, computer-science/frontier-literature and engineering/development reports, challenged in cross-review.\n- Propose one jointly trained artifact with exact event memory, learned geometric candidate admission, mutable relative-frame energy, shared sparse state operators and normalized sparse Generate/Copy/Stop output, alongside a competent ordinary arm.\n- Define exact-history capacity, causal hard routing and credit assignment, Copy/Generate likelihood boundaries, numerical/access budgets, training checkpoint costs and a complete language/memory/code roadmap.\n- Update canonical navigation while preserving owner decisions D0-b and D4–D6 and all earlier negative results.\n\n## Evidence and boundaries\n\nReviewed source: `3101c06061726d9438a22649a25b98558525e8d0`; protected main at review: `552d847d49fb263966165004b835f2f53cccaae1`. This PR is intentionally stacked on #1384 (`codex/native-sparse-read-20260924`); #1380–#1384 were open, not merged. The new model is a proposal: no implementation, training, model replay, geometric advantage or energy result is claimed. No stable policy is changed. Original checkout and unique artifacts are preserved.\n\n## Executed validation\n\n- `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py` — passed.\n- `git diff --cached --check` — passed.\n- All 76 local links in the five new review documents resolve.\n- Mermaid structured creation and static lint pass for the canonical source and embedded diagram. This is not renderer acceptance.\n\nNo Cargo build or model tests were run because this PR only changes research/planning documents and navigation. Historical CI status names remain compatibility acknowledgements, not executed test results. The review packet records resource scope and final closeout.\n\n## Next development milestone\n\nOne integrated learned attention-language artifact, including the ordinary/geometric comparison, source-conditioned uncopied generation, exact history and full-path sparse-access accounting. Freeze acceptance and complete resource projections before the fresh evaluation/training launch. No further tuning of the exposed metadata gate is proposed.\n",
